                <pb facs="0141" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.51 Struma Valley/2d: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-14T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 14,
                                1928—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4. Department’s 2, January 12, 10 a.m. Department understands that Monks-Ulen
                    proposal is the only one from American concerns <pb facs="0142" n="32"
                        xml:id="pg32"/> for Struma Valley drainage. If such is not the case you will
                    of course bear in mind Department’s policy of strict impartiality between
                    competing American concerns.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olds</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
